pagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content #{}, :strongest #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "4c024f19-d4e3-3b6f-b19e-36c29c7c605f"} #propagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content #{}, :strongest #{}}}, :dict {:slot-index {}, :base #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "607b0478-b17f-3064-a59f-22ff67761fef"}, :support #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "e6aed8d1-d368-3083-8fdb-2ddee4c4dc7f"}, :membership #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "04534c0f-69db-3ab8-aee6-94c395136f33"}, :premise-state #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "4c024f19-d4e3-3b6f-b19e-36c29c7c605f"}}, :relationship {}}, [[:outer] #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "dc373e3b-bf2e-315d-875c-331bc51f942f"}] #propagators.network.Net{:graph {#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fc8b4fe0-73e1-30ee-a925-a195d6527e59"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "94853eba-fba3-33bc-9ce4-a12e98a7308d"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "a3d0bacb-3c02-3d5d-bf1e-b2f36ffb4e21"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}}, :env {#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fc8b4fe0-73e1-30ee-a925-a195d6527e59"} #propagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content {:kind :reply, :text "", :thinking "Let me analyze the context carefully. I need to construct a small live conversation network in Lain. Let me understand the key constraints:\n\n1. Lain is a dataflow language, not Clojure\n2. `(-> x f)` writes to a cell, doesn't call f\n3. `(f x)` calls a callable\n4. Use `seq:empty` and `seq:append` for vectors\n5. `event:point` captures temporal occurrences\n6. `behavior:source` creates a reducer cell\n7. `behavior:scan` accumulates occurrences\n8. `behavior:latest-value` projects a behavior to ordinary value\n9. `model:request` is a function that must be invoked, not used as connection target\n10. `message-to-user` acknowledges a record\n11. `user-ingress` publishes a recor