ary with actual events; constants user/1 and assistant/2 cannot identify three turns. A bare acknowledged record must be converted to a temporal occurrence before feeding a temporal source. A callable inside behavior:map or scan is evaluated as a pure transformation; model:request and message-to-user must run in the live network, never inside a temporal transformation callback. seq:map with key :role returns strings and therefore is unsuitable as the request messages vector. No generated definitions from previous attempts exist in this fresh child.\"} {:title \"context-cell\", :reference #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid \"302c51ff-677a-372f-a1ba-95c01e259135\"}, :state :known, :headline \"Construct a small live conversation network in Lain. Keep reasoning brief. Return only executable Lain forms, without markdown. Discover the environment bindings below. Your setup must build history with the supplied tested temporal reducers, preserving chronological user messages and acknowledged assistant replies. Connect user-ingress to model requests and define a reusable reply function that delivers to the user, then adds the acknowledged reply to history. Subsequent requests must contain actual prior user messages and delivered assistant replies as role-tagged messages. Provider thinking and generated source are never conversation replies. Each subsequent model response must be executable Lain calling your reply function with a new assistant message. Conversation requests should include an explicit system message containing the reply-function calling convention you have defined, so future requests know to produce executable source. Do not include setup code or provider thinking in conversation history. Use the same model throughout. Do not send a request until a user event arrives. Unknown inputs suspend a computation; avoid cycles requiring a future reply before the first request. model:request is a function and must be invoked, not used as a connection target. Inspect diagnostics if construction fails.\"}]"}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "94853eba-fba3-33bc-9ce4-a12e98a7308d"} #propagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content #{{:source #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "c2e15b94-dfa4-3283-94e4-b94c166c821d"}, :timestamp 4, :premises-status :active}}, :strongest #{{:source #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "c2e15b94-dfa4-3283-94e4-b94c166c821d"}, :timestamp 4, :premises-status :active}}}}, :dict {:slot-index {:base #{}, :support #{}}, :base #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "fc8b4fe0-73e1-30ee-a925-a195d6527e59"}, :support #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "94853eba-fba3-33bc-9ce4-a12e98a7308d"}}, :relationship {}}, [[:outer] #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "1d8366ba-4c35-3c90-a568-1ed9f58e4311"}] {:gur.flat/recursive-closure? true, :compiler-2/declaration #propagators.network.Net{:graph {#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808b9"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808ba"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808bb"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808bc"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808bd"} #propagators.graph.Node{:inputs #{}, :outputs #{}}}, :env {#propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808b9"} #propagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "0329c240-ffed-3b76-830e-d516150eefea"}, :strongest #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "0329c240-ffed-3b76-830e-d516150eefea"}}, #propagators.ids.NodeId{:uuid #uuid "01a1a91e-cc55-7e39-926b-f65fc9c808ba"} #propagators.cells.cell.Cell{:name :cell/anonymous, :content #propagators.network.Net{:graph {#propagators.id